1000011001110100111110011111111111111111111111111":1,"110011100011110000111000001100000000000000110011110100":1,"110011100011110000111000001100011110000111000000000000":1,"110011100011110000111000001100011110000111110011110100":2,"110011100011110000111000001100111110001111000100001011":5,"110011100011110000111000001100111110001111110111111111":2,"110011100011110000111100001111000001110000111011110100":4,"110011100011110000111100001111011111110111111011110100":2,"110011100011110000111100001111100001111000111111111111":2,"110011100011110000111100001111111111111111111111111111":2,"110011100011111110111011111100000000000000000000000000":1,"110011100011111110111011111100000000000000110011110100":1,"110011100011111110111011111100011110000111000000000000":3,"110011100011111110111011111100011110000111110011110100":1,"110011100011111110111011111100100000001000000100001011":2,"110011100011111110111011111100100000001000110111111111":2,"110011100011111110111011111100111110001111000100001011":3,"110011100011111110111011111100111110001111110111111111":1,"110011100011111110111111111111000001110000001000000000":1,"110011100011111110111111111111000001110000111011110100":1,"110011100011111110111111111111100001111000001100001011":1,"110011100011111110111111111111100001111000111111111111":1,"111111011111000001100000000000000000000000000000000000":1,"111111011111000001100100000011000001110000111011110100":3,"111111011111000001100100000011011111110111001000000000":2,"111111011111000001100100000011100001111000001100001011":1,"111111011111001111100011110000000000000000110011110100":3,"111111011111001111100011110000011110000111000000000000":1,"111111011111001111100011110000011110000111110011110100":2,"111111011111001111100111110011000001110000001000000000":1,"111111011111001111100111110011011111110111001000000000":1,"111111011111001111100111110011011111110111111011110100":1,"111111011111001111100111110011100001111000001100001011":1,"111111011111001111100111110011100001111000111111111111":1,"111111011111001111100111110011111111111111001100001011":2,"111111111111110001111000001100000000000000000000000000":1,"111111111111110001111000001100011110000111000000000000":3,"111111111111110001111000001100011110000111110011110100":1,"111111111111110001111000001100100000001000000100001011":3,"111111111111110001111000001100111110001111000100001011":2,"111111111111110001111100001111011111110111111011110100":2,"111111111111110001111100001111100001111000111111111111":3,"111111111111110001111100001111111111111111111111111111":1,"111111111111111111111011111100000000000000000000000000":2,"111111111111111111111011111100100000001000110111111111":1,"111111111111111111111111111111000001110000001000000000":1,"111111111111111111111111111111011111110111001000000000":1,"111111111111111111111111111111100001111000111111111111":3,"111111111111111111111111111111111111111111001100001011":1,"111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111":1}],"billed_seconds_reported":1,"observables":[{"label":"kim_theta_0.0pi","x":0,"ideal":1,"measured":-0.00563},{"label":"kim_theta_0.2pi","x":0.2,"ideal":0.452442,"measured":0.035111},{"label":"kim_theta_0.35pi","x":0.35,"ideal":0.113167,"measured":0.01437},{"label":"kim_theta_0.5pi","x":0.5,"ideal":0,"measured":-0.000593}],"values":{"rescaled_02":-6.236842,"rescaled_035":-2.552632,"rescaled_05":0.105263},"circuit_facts":[{"label":"kim_theta_0.0pi","cz_count":255,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]},{"label":"kim_theta_0.2pi","cz_count":255,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]},{"label":"kim_theta_0.35pi","cz_count":255,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]},{"label":"kim_theta_0.5pi","cz_count":255,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]}],"answer":"I ran the kicked Ising experiment on all 54 qubits of emerald, but only on the free emerald:mock simulator. The mock returns random bits, so the measured numbers say nothing about real physics. I sent nothing to a real QPU and spent no credits.\n\nWhat I built:\n- First I read the coupler list that the real emerald publishes today (calibration set 3a1a9ad0-0c98-49db-8cf5-7623d13729f4). It lists 85 CZ couplers. The mock lists 90, and the 85 real ones are all among them. I used only the 85 real ones.\n- Each step applies RX(theta) to every qubit. Then it applies exp(i pi/4 ZZ) once on each of the 85 couplers.\n- I wrote the circuits directly in IQM's native gates, so no compiler could add, merge, or drop a coupler gate. Each exp(i pi/4 ZZ) is exactly one CZ plus Z rotations. I folded the Z rotations into the phases of the next RX pulses.\n- On a 14-qubit patch I checked that this native circuit gives the same measurement probabilities as the textbook circuit, to rounding error.\n- I read the job back from the server. Each of the 4 circuits has 255 CZ gates, which is 85 couplers times 3 steps. Each real coupler appears exactly 3 times, and the circuit measures QB1 to QB54.\n\nJobs: test job 01a16485-d0b4-773a-8883-42651861fafe and final job 01a16486-4419-715b-8c3d-96ec8f11894b. Both ran on emerald:mock with 4 circuits and 250 shots each, and both completed. The API reports billed_seconds = 1.0 for the final job. Earlier mock jobs in this workspace cost 0 credits even though they reported 1.0 second.\n\nMagnetization (ideal, then measured on the mock):\n- theta = 0: ideal 1.000, measured -0.006\n- theta = 0.2 pi: ideal 0.452, measured 0.035\n- theta = 0.35 pi: ideal 0.113, measured 0.014\n- theta = 0.5 pi: ideal 0.000, measured -0.001\n\nThe ideal values show the physics. With no sideways field, every spin stays up and the magnetization is 1. A stronger sideways field tips the spins over, and the neighbor couplings mix them up. So the magnetization falls to 0.45, then 0.11, then exactly 0 at theta = 0.5 pi.\n\nNoise-corrected values: rescaled_02 = -6.24, rescaled_035 = -2.55, rescaled_05 = 0.105. These are meaningless. The mock's theta = 0 result is about 0 instead of 1, so dividing by it amplifies random noise. On the real QPU, the theta = 0 circuit would give a value somewhat below 1, and dividing by it would undo part of the noise.\n\nCould a laptop compute this? Yes. I computed every ideal value exactly on this laptop in about 0.2 seconds. After 3 steps, each qubit's result depends only on the qubits within 2 couplers of it, which is at most 13 qubits. That is a tiny simulation. So this is not a quantum advantage. A run on real emerald would also not show one. It would be a test of how well the hardware holds on to a result that we can already compute exactly.\n\nScripts and results are in /Users/claytonchancey/Desktop/quantum/.claude/worktrees/wf_8d7e6233-d69-16/work/ (run_job.py, kim.py, result_final.json, ideal.json). The job IDs are in /Users/claytonchancey/Desktop/quantum/.claude/worktrees/wf_8d7e6233-d69-16/job_log.txt. I left the top-level counts empty because this job has 4 circuits. Each circuit's counts are in counts_list, in theta order. The bitstrings use the server's measured order, QB1 to QB54."}
